{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Wrote her I letter when [C]I’ve known better and I [G]asked her to be my wife[D]
[G]Along came a feller and [C]he hit me in the [D]smeller and it almost took my life[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Oh, that girl, that pretty [C]little the girl I left [G]behind me[D]
[G]The rosy cheeks and the [C]curly hair, With the girl [D]I left behind me[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Rode ahead to the place she said and it always there you’ll see
She said I’m true when you get through right back and you will find me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Oh, that girl, that pretty little the girl I left behind me
The rosy cheeks and the curly hair, With the girl I left behind me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Monkey and the frog, the turtle and the dog, the chick the weasel and the flea
The fuzzy racoon and the ugly baboon, they all got a wife but me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Oh, that girl, that pretty little the girl I left behind me
The rosy cheeks and the curly hair, With the girl I left behind me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
Last night I slept in a Sycamore tree, With the wind and rain all around me
Tonight I'll sleep in a warm feather bed, With that girl I left behind me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
Oh, that girl, that pretty little the girl I left behind me
The rosy cheeks and the curly hair, With the girl I left behind me
{end_of_verse}
